00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:47.460
"In my school, a girl wanted to commit suicide. A lot of people including myself were laughing

00:00:47.679 --> 00:00:49.679
because we thought that she was joking.

00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:52.619
She ended up doing it. I regret it."

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.909
"All my friends are very smart.

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:24.129
I came from a gifted program in middle school and ended up failing multiple classes in the past three years.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.799
I've managed to hide this from my parents.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:34.780
Only one person knows about my failed suicide attempts, stemming from my academic problems, and the constant berating from my parents."

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:40.299
"I'm really struggling to find my identity, and it feels as though,

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:45.669
everyone around me already knows theirs, almost like I'll never find who I really am."

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:54.159
"My friends all think that I'm happy 24/7. Yeah, I am miserable. Every minute of every day.

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:58.809
I feel like an outsider. I always make sure they are okay.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:05.949
Yet, no one asked me if I am. I feel as though I can't talk to my friends. They wouldn't understand,

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:09.310
but they are the only people that I have."

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:14.859
"I used to listen to my parents fight every day when they thought I was asleep.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:21.130
This made it hard for me to do things with my parents, because I knew that they were fighting."

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:25.329
Yeah, I grew up with both my parents and

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:28.090
I was always like embarrassed of that,

00:02:28.459 --> 00:02:34.809
because a lot of the people that were in my school or my neighborhood didn't have both parents, but my parents fought a lot.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:42.489
I resented my father for his anger and his frustration. I resented my mother for being sick and all of our money going towards

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.540
health care and,

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:50.019
and as a family you don't talk about often, because it's not, you're like, this is nobody's business what we're arguing about. We're good,

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:52.388
we're happy family. Look at all these pictures look at us, you know,

00:02:53.989 --> 00:02:57.099
but it does it does affect you,  it does make it difficult.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:03.100
"I am extremely self-conscious about my looks. There has been a time where I felt so ugly,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:08.109
I considered ending my life because I thought if I wasn't pretty, there was no reason to be here."

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.539
This would have been my confession four years ago.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:18.670
Not many people know, but I have attempted suicide

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.190
four times in my life,

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.769
because of the mental health issues that I have

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:29.600
struggled with and that I have dealt with in my life, and I'm so glad that

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.040
none of my attempts

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:37.279
were successful. I'm so happy that I'm here. Sometimes when you're in this headspace, you can be

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.330
deaf to

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:46.100
hearing people talk about who you are as a person, because all you care about is your appearance, and how you look, and it's

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:49.969
easier said than done to say that you shouldn't focus on that, but

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:55.700
it's true. And if you look at the people around you, people will believe that you're beautiful for who you are, and

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.210
ending your life just is not the answer at all.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:09.799
"I was sexually molested by another classmate about four years ago, and I still can't find the courage to tell my parents.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:16.250
Even if this happened four years ago, I still feel guilty for everything that happened."

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:24.739
I was molested growing up, and so I know that there is a lot of shame that you can carry, but

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:31.309
the longer that you hold that in, and you don't talk to someone about that, that guilt and that shame, it's going to

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:36.379
consume you, even if you feel like you're managing it, okay, it can turn into anxiety.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:41.479
It can haunt you in the night, and you have to talk to somebody about that. I know that there's a lot of fear,

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:48.619
especially about being believed, and how people will react, but like I believe you, and it is not your fault.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:57.710
"Whenever my parents compared me to other kids because of how much better they are, I think of wanting to vanish or run away,

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.260
because they deserve a better child."

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.950
Okay,

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.977
I should read this aloud, sorry.

00:05:08.977 --> 00:05:12.589
"I bullied my transitioning best friend until he killed himself.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:20.540
After he died, I felt terrible. I couldn't sleep, couldn't eat, and to this day, carry the burden of his death on my shoulders.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.420
I regret it, but I never told anyone."

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:31.939
"It started in seventh grade. I was bullied. Extremely insecure, simply just not happy.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:37.159
I had been cutting, starving, whatever I could do to punish myself for being me."

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.840
Reminds me of my past,

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.720
way before I was even born.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:55.339
The doctors had told my parents that "That child has a 5% chance of survival," and throughout those surgeries,

00:05:55.340 --> 00:06:00.200
I ended up having so many scars all over my body and they told me you know, "Janice,

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.749
those are your battle scars, you know, they're beautiful.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:09.440
They're amazing, and you should be proud of them." When I went into kindergarten, went into elementary school, my first nickname

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.560
was, "broken doll"

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:19.639
second one being Frankenstein's monster. Because of that, I became bulimic for a few months.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:27.739
I cut my arm a few times. I just kept punishing myself. I kept on pressuring myself to be this perfect person,

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.590
no matter the cost.

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:36.890
I realized what I was doing was wrong. I realized that the image that my parents

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:45.960
wanted me in my head of myself was broken, and shattered, and thrown away by myself. As my parents said, my scars are beautiful,

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.340
I'm beautiful.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:51.349
Everyone is made, just exactly as they were meant to be.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.250
There's other ways to

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:59.510
release any emotion or pain. I journal, I

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.660
go on little adventures by myself,

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.700
listening to music, singing when no one's around,

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.360
crying is one of the biggest ones.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.049
You won't be 13 forever. Your relationship will change

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:20.270
with your parents, their relationship with themselves, and with their own traumas will change and adapt. They're humans,

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:22.820
they're superhuman,

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.860
often to a fault, and

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:30.109
they care about you, and they're trying.
- Being okay with who you are is

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.890
the most important thing, and then

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:38.299
feeling appreciated by those around you comes should come second,

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:43.729
it shouldn't be first.
- A lot of the people that seem like they have it all figured out, probably don't,

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:46.100
so just be patient with yourself, and

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.770
just keep doing things that you enjoy, and

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:53.719
discovering who you are, and know that it might take time, and that you can go at your own pace.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:58.369
It doesn't matter where you're at right now. It's your journey. It's not anyone else's.

